# Intentionally near-empty. Without this file, npm falls back to using
# .gitignore's patterns as its own pack-time ignore rules for git-based
# installs (e.g. `npx github:ken2san/project-template`) — which also
# silently drops .gitignore itself from the installed package despite it
# being listed in package.json's "files", breaking init-project.sh's
# `cp .gitignore` step on every npx run. Having any .npmignore, even an
# empty one, disables that fallback.
